cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it using these metadata."

title: "Sequential Reciprocal Matching Under Uncertainty: code and data"
type: software

abstract: >-
  Code and data for a two-phase study of policy evaluation in sequential
  reciprocal matching under a rare outcome. Phase 1 screened seventeen policy
  configurations on ten seeds and reported that one beat the supplied greedy
  baseline by +0.175 MSMI per 100 arrived members (95% seed-block CI
  [+0.092, +0.258], p = 0.016). Phase 2 recovered that configuration from
  surviving code, confirmed it reproduces the published headline exactly
  (0.525 and 63 events, matching on 60 of 60 episodes), and re-tested it on
  120 fresh seeds. The advantage did not replicate: the configuration scored
  0.3694 against the baseline's 0.4021, a paired difference of 0.0326 in the
  baseline's favour (95% CI [-0.0250, +0.0903], p = 0.356), with the two
  estimates 7.09 standard errors apart. The repository contains the simulator
  interface, all policy arms, the experiment harness, the statistics module,
  and the raw per-episode records from which every reported number can be
  recomputed.

